<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Philip of Saint-Pol</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1404">1404</a>–<a href="/years/1430">1430</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a> · Also known as Philip I, Duke of Brabant</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Philip of Saint-Pol was duke of Brabant and Limburg from 1427 until his death in 1430, the younger son of Duke Antoine. Count of Saint-Pol and Ligny before succeeding his brother John IV, he was made regent of Brabant by the estates in 1420 during their quarrel with John. He died unmarried, and the duchy passed to his cousin <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/philip-the-good">Philip the Good</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/burgundy">Burgundy</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/philip-of-saint-pol.jpg" alt="Philip of Saint-Pol" width="179" height="228" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Antonio de Succa · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Filip_SAint_Pol.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
